// The spent-voucher record in the directory (DESIGN §9, F5): what deleting a
// host does to it, what a failed join does to it, and which server writes it.
//
// A voucher carries a salt and names a home server. kuipad accepts a salt once:
// `Slot(salt, 'fresh')` is the absence of a record for it and `Slot(salt,
// 'spent')` its presence, one token per salt that a join moves from fresh to
// spent, a rollback moves back, and a purge removes. `Alive(salt)` is the
// voucher's validity window.
//
// The token is the home server's directory entry. Any server may take a join (the
// redeemer, `$r` in the actions), but it asks the home server to spend the salt
// first, so every attempt for a salt goes through the one token and two servers
// cannot each accept the voucher before their directories replicate.
// peer-voucher-spent-previous.spthy models the earlier design with a token per
// directory, where they can.
//
// The previous code also kept the record on the host entry, so deleting the host
// freed the salt, and released it after any failure; the controls model that too.
// Current code writes one record per salt (ipaKUVoucherSpentRecord) that outlives
// the host: `host_delete` removes the host entry only. A purge removes a record
// once the voucher can no longer verify (`expire`, then `purge`).
//
// A join is `join_add` (the home server's record and the host entry written; the
// join is `Pending`), then `group_ok`, or a failure. A failed join keeps the record
// unless the host is certainly absent: `group_fails_rollback` (the host delete
// succeeded, and the redeemer has the home server release the record) releases the
// salt; a lost reply from the host add, or a host delete that fails
// (`group_fails_host_remains`), keep it. A join the home server answered ok for
// and that is then refused with no host made has the record released, and changes
// nothing, so it is not a step.
//
// Omitted: the signature and the join's key exchange (kuipa.spthy VoucherSingleUse
// owns those), the lease, the voucher's validity check at the join, the request
// that spends and the one that releases (their authentication is the peer-sync
// kind: see the Kerberos-bound channel in DESIGN §9), a repeated spend (the home
// server refuses every repeat), the best-effort release after an unanswered spend,
// and a release by a redeemer other than the one that spent: no rule allows it,
// and the home server refuses it in kuipad.
//
// Run 2026-11-13, Tamarin 1.12.0, Maude 3.5.1, proofs.sh -t 400 (8 GiB), one lemma
// per process.
// Verified: join_then_delete, purge_after_join, rollback_then_other_server,
// host_remains_reachable (reachability); rollback_by_redeemer;
// second_host_needs_rollback; salt_single_use (uses second_host_needs_rollback as
// a source, [reuse], which verifies on its own); purge_only_after_expiry.
// Open: none.
theory peer_voucher_spent
begin

rule issue:
  [ Fr(~salt) ]
  --[ Issued(~salt) ]->
  [ Slot(~salt, 'fresh'), Alive(~salt) ]

// A redeemer, the server that takes a join, asks the voucher's home server to
// spend the salt and adds the host entry when the home server answers ok
// (kuipad's join in directory.rs). Only the home server writes the record:
// `Slot` is its one token for the salt, the directory entry, and it names the
// redeemer the record was written for. The two steps are one here: a join that
// the home server answered ok for and then refused, with no host made, has the
// record released and is a step that changes nothing. `Pending` is the join
// between the host add and the group update.
rule join_add:
  [ Slot(salt, 'fresh'), Fr(~host) ]
  --[ HomeSpent(salt, $r), HostCreated(salt, ~host, $r) ]->
  [ Slot(salt, 'spent'), Host(~host, salt), Pending(~host, salt, $r) ]

// The group update succeeds and the join is done.
rule group_ok:
  [ Pending(host, salt, r) ]
  --[ Joined(salt, host) ]->
  [ ]

// The group update fails and the host delete succeeds: the voucher enrolled
// no one and the redeemer has the record released, so a retry can work.
rule group_fails_rollback:
  [ Pending(host, salt, r), Host(host, salt), Slot(salt, 'spent') ]
  --[ RolledBack(salt, host, r) ]->
  [ Slot(salt, 'fresh') ]

// The group update fails and the host delete fails too, or the host add
// committed but reported an error: a host may exist. The redeemer does not
// ask for a release and the record stays.
rule group_fails_host_remains:
  [ Pending(host, salt, r) ]
  --[ HostRemains(salt, host) ]->
  [ ]

// Current code: the host goes, the record stays.
rule host_delete:
  [ Host(host, salt) ]
  --[ HostDeleted(host, salt) ]->
  [ ]

// The window closes. An unused voucher lapses with it; a spent one leaves its
// record waiting to be purged.
rule expire:
  [ Alive(salt) ]
  --[ Expired(salt) ]->
  [ Closed(salt) ]

rule lapse:
  [ Closed(salt), Slot(salt, 'fresh') ]
  --[ Lapsed(salt) ]->
  [ ]

rule purge:
  [ Closed(salt), Slot(salt, 'spent') ]
  --[ Purged(salt) ]->
  [ ]

// Reachability: a voucher enrols a host that is then deleted; a failed group
// update rolls back and another server takes the salt.
lemma join_then_delete: exists-trace
  "Ex salt host #i #j. Joined(salt, host) @i & HostDeleted(host, salt) @j & #i < #j"
lemma purge_after_join: exists-trace
  "Ex salt host #i #j. Joined(salt, host) @i & Purged(salt) @j & #i < #j"
lemma rollback_then_other_server: exists-trace
  "Ex salt h1 h2 #i #j #k. HostCreated(salt, h1, 'A') @i & RolledBack(salt, h1, 'A') @j & HostCreated(salt, h2, 'B') @k & #j < #k"
lemma host_remains_reachable: exists-trace
  "Ex salt host #i. HostRemains(salt, host) @i"

// A rollback releases the record of the redeemer that made the host, and no
// other redeemer's: the token names the redeemer it was spent for.
lemma rollback_by_redeemer:
  "All salt h r #i. RolledBack(salt, h, r) @i ==> Ex #j. HostCreated(salt, h, r) @j & HomeSpent(salt, r) @j & #j < #i"

// A second host is created for a salt, by any server, only after the first was
// cleanly rolled back; a lost reply, a failed delete or an administrator's
// host-del never makes the salt usable again.
lemma second_host_needs_rollback [use_induction, reuse]:
  "All salt h1 h2 r1 r2 #i #j. HostCreated(salt, h1, r1) @i & HostCreated(salt, h2, r2) @j & #i < #j
     ==> Ex #k. RolledBack(salt, h1, r1) @k & #i < #k & #k < #j"

// A salt completes a join at most once, whatever happens to the host in between.
// A corollary of the lemma above, which it uses as a source: the first host's
// rollback consumes the join before it can complete.
lemma salt_single_use:
  "All salt h1 h2 #i #j. Joined(salt, h1) @i & Joined(salt, h2) @j ==> #i = #j"

// A record is purged only after the voucher's window closed, so a purge never
// makes a still-valid voucher usable again.
lemma purge_only_after_expiry:
  "All salt #i. Purged(salt) @i ==> Ex #j. Expired(salt) @j & #j < #i"
end
